Subject: Net Tech

[in which Vince forsees a world in which everything looks like a
folder on his desktop]

This really is not too difficult to do today. All you need is
an NFS server that does what you want with your mail files. There are
several good examples of small NFS servers on the net, including the
amd automounter and hlfsd, both available via ftp at cs.columbia.edu.
What's really nice about this solution is that it requires _no_ work
on the mac; as far as the mac is concerned, it's just mounting an NFS
volume from some server. 

The main problem I see is authentication. NFS has this very weak
security model in which trusting clients is essentially an
all-or-nothing proposition. If I have control over a machine (like a
Mac) I can pretend to be whomever I want. You might not want to make
your mailboxes acessible to whoever can spoof your iP address.

-Rens

