  I have added a new functionality to ::resend which is range. The new
command has argument form:

::resend range1,range2,...,range_n

Each range is either a single message number, or two message numbers
separated by a hyphen, the first number being the start message, the
second being the ending message.

e.g.

::resend #80,#94-1-93-#94-1-110

(resend message 80, and messages 93 through 110)
  The '#' MUST be present as always and is especially important here
since the list software must be able to find out how to break up the
range. (the '-' is overloaded)

More examples

::resend #94-1-81,#110-#130
::resend #81,#82,#83

 If you request only 1 message, it will arrive as a single message. If
you request more than one, you will get them in digest format.


  I want to make a change to the digestification format which adds an
